{
  "schema_version": "1.0",
  "encounter_id": "00230",
  "segments": [
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0001",
      "speaker_id": "person_1",
      "role": "NURSE",
      "start_seconds": 0.85,
      "end_seconds": 8.57,
      "duration_seconds": 7.72,
      "text": "Doctor, the patient's with us now. I did the usual checks at the front, so just say when you want them."
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0002",
      "speaker_id": "person_2",
      "role": "DOCTOR",
      "start_seconds": 9.47,
      "end_seconds": 13.06,
      "duration_seconds": 3.59,
      "text": "Great. Hello, come in and sit down. How can I help?"
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0003",
      "speaker_id": "person_3",
      "role": "PATIENT",
      "start_seconds": 13.57,
      "end_seconds": 22.49,
      "duration_seconds": 8.92,
      "text": "Well, doctor, it's very heavy periods. It's getting on my nerves now. I didn't want to make a fuss, you know."
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0004",
      "speaker_id": "person_2",
      "role": "DOCTOR",
      "start_seconds": 23.72,
      "end_seconds": 25.98,
      "duration_seconds": 2.26,
      "text": "How long has this been going on?"
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0005",
      "speaker_id": "person_3",
      "role": "PATIENT",
      "start_seconds": 26.97,
      "end_seconds": 29.94,
      "duration_seconds": 2.97,
      "text": "I've had it for about four days."
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0006",
      "speaker_id": "person_2",
      "role": "DOCTOR",
      "start_seconds": 31.12,
      "end_seconds": 34.07,
      "duration_seconds": 2.95,
      "text": "On a normal day, how strong is it?"
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0007",
      "speaker_id": "person_3",
      "role": "PATIENT",
      "start_seconds": 35.42,
      "end_seconds": 46.48,
      "duration_seconds": 11.06,
      "text": "Hmm, I'd give it a seven, out of ten. I've also been passing clots, for six months. I had tiredness before. That's settled now, though."
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0008",
      "speaker_id": "person_2",
      "role": "DOCTOR",
      "start_seconds": 47.23,
      "end_seconds": 49.77,
      "duration_seconds": 2.54,
      "text": "Let me just write this down properly."
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0009",
      "speaker_id": "person_2",
      "role": "DOCTOR",
      "start_seconds": 62.67,
      "end_seconds": 67.52,
      "duration_seconds": 4.85,
      "text": "Okay, that's done. Right, any pain during sex, weight loss or fever?"
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0010",
      "speaker_id": "person_3",
      "role": "PATIENT",
      "start_seconds": 68.68,
      "end_seconds": 72.69,
      "duration_seconds": 4.01,
      "text": "No, no pain during sex, weight loss or fever."
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0011",
      "speaker_id": "person_2",
      "role": "DOCTOR",
      "start_seconds": 74.09,
      "end_seconds": 76.09,
      "duration_seconds": 2.0,
      "text": "And vaginal discharge, any of that?"
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0012",
      "speaker_id": "person_3",
      "role": "PATIENT",
      "start_seconds": 77.48,
      "end_seconds": 79.61,
      "duration_seconds": 2.13,
      "text": "No vaginal discharge, thank goodness."
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0013",
      "speaker_id": "person_2",
      "role": "DOCTOR",
      "start_seconds": 80.37,
      "end_seconds": 83.61,
      "duration_seconds": 3.24,
      "text": "What about your tummy and bowels, anything unusual there?"
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0014",
      "speaker_id": "person_3",
      "role": "PATIENT",
      "start_seconds": 84.81,
      "end_seconds": 87.43,
      "duration_seconds": 2.62,
      "text": "No, you know, all normal there."
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0015",
      "speaker_id": "person_2",
      "role": "DOCTOR",
      "start_seconds": 88.65,
      "end_seconds": 90.64,
      "duration_seconds": 1.99,
      "text": "Your breathing, any trouble there?"
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0016",
      "speaker_id": "person_3",
      "role": "PATIENT",
      "start_seconds": 91.4,
      "end_seconds": 93.21,
      "duration_seconds": 1.81,
      "text": "No problems with breathing."
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0017",
      "speaker_id": "person_2",
      "role": "DOCTOR",
      "start_seconds": 94.75,
      "end_seconds": 99.07,
      "duration_seconds": 4.32,
      "text": "What about family history, any illnesses that run in the family?"
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0018",
      "speaker_id": "person_3",
      "role": "PATIENT",
      "start_seconds": 100.54,
      "end_seconds": 105.18,
      "duration_seconds": 4.64,
      "text": "My mother had high blood pressure. My father had kidney stones."
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0019",
      "speaker_id": "person_2",
      "role": "DOCTOR",
      "start_seconds": 106.19,
      "end_seconds": 109.06,
      "duration_seconds": 2.87,
      "text": "Do you have any questions before we carry on?"
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0020",
      "speaker_id": "person_3",
      "role": "PATIENT",
      "start_seconds": 109.81,
      "end_seconds": 120.76,
      "duration_seconds": 10.95,
      "text": "Not at the moment, I think you've covered most of what I was wondering. If something comes to mind later, I'll ask you before I leave."
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0021",
      "speaker_id": "person_2",
      "role": "DOCTOR",
      "start_seconds": 121.42,
      "end_seconds": 125.13,
      "duration_seconds": 3.71,
      "text": "What about allergies, to medicines or foods or anything else?"
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0022",
      "speaker_id": "person_3",
      "role": "PATIENT",
      "start_seconds": 125.44,
      "end_seconds": 129.03,
      "duration_seconds": 3.59,
      "text": "Sulfa drugs. I come out in... well, a rash."
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0023",
      "speaker_id": "person_2",
      "role": "DOCTOR",
      "start_seconds": 130.1,
      "end_seconds": 133.26,
      "duration_seconds": 3.16,
      "text": "Do you have everything you need to get home alright?"
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0024",
      "speaker_id": "person_3",
      "role": "PATIENT",
      "start_seconds": 134.67,
      "end_seconds": 147.23,
      "duration_seconds": 12.56,
      "text": "Yes, I've got my transport sorted. It's a bit of a trek, but I'm used to the journey by now, and I brought something to read for the wait."
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0025",
      "speaker_id": "person_2",
      "role": "DOCTOR",
      "start_seconds": 147.83,
      "end_seconds": 151.21,
      "duration_seconds": 3.38,
      "text": "Moving on to your background, any past medical history?"
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0026",
      "speaker_id": "person_3",
      "role": "PATIENT",
      "start_seconds": 154.52,
      "end_seconds": 169.41,
      "duration_seconds": 14.89,
      "text": "I've had an underactive thyroid, yes. I thought it would sort itself out, but it hasn't. I wasn't sure whether to come in at all, to be honest. Oh, yes, diabetes. It's the not knowing that gets to me."
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0027",
      "speaker_id": "person_2",
      "role": "DOCTOR",
      "start_seconds": 170.21,
      "end_seconds": 179.77,
      "duration_seconds": 9.56,
      "text": "Yes, I can see the an underactive thyroid in your file as well. Yes, I can see the diabetes in your file as well. Right, any previous surgeries?"
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0028",
      "speaker_id": "person_3",
      "role": "PATIENT",
      "start_seconds": 180.1,
      "end_seconds": 187.62,
      "duration_seconds": 7.52,
      "text": "Oh, just my gallbladder removed, in 2016. A neighbour of mine said I should see someone about it."
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0029",
      "speaker_id": "person_2",
      "role": "DOCTOR",
      "start_seconds": 188.7,
      "end_seconds": 190.87,
      "duration_seconds": 2.17,
      "text": "I'll just check what's already recorded here."
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0030",
      "speaker_id": "person_3",
      "role": "PATIENT",
      "start_seconds": 191.34,
      "end_seconds": 192.11,
      "duration_seconds": 0.77,
      "text": "Please do."
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0031",
      "speaker_id": "person_2",
      "role": "DOCTOR",
      "start_seconds": 201.26,
      "end_seconds": 205.56,
      "duration_seconds": 4.3,
      "text": "Alright, I've got it. Are you on any tablets or medication?"
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0032",
      "speaker_id": "person_3",
      "role": "PATIENT",
      "start_seconds": 206.29,
      "end_seconds": 210.39,
      "duration_seconds": 4.1,
      "text": "Right, I'm on Glycomet, 500 milligrams, twice a day."
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0033",
      "speaker_id": "person_1",
      "role": "NURSE",
      "start_seconds": 211.59,
      "end_seconds": 215.8,
      "duration_seconds": 4.21,
      "text": "Doctor, our chart from the last visit lists it as 250 milligrams."
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0034",
      "speaker_id": "person_2",
      "role": "DOCTOR",
      "start_seconds": 216.2,
      "end_seconds": 219.52,
      "duration_seconds": 3.32,
      "text": "I see. Is the most recent prescription on you?"
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0035",
      "speaker_id": "person_3",
      "role": "PATIENT",
      "start_seconds": 220.23,
      "end_seconds": 229.18,
      "duration_seconds": 8.95,
      "text": "Right, no, I left it at home. Mefenamic acid. I take it 500 milligrams, when the pain is bad."
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0036",
      "speaker_id": "person_1",
      "role": "NURSE",
      "start_seconds": 230.75,
      "end_seconds": 240.97,
      "duration_seconds": 10.22,
      "text": "Okay, so the vitals from earlier. Pulse is 68 beats a minute, SpO2 97 percent on room air, temperature is 36.9 degrees. Pressure 117 over 74."
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0037",
      "speaker_id": "person_2",
      "role": "DOCTOR",
      "start_seconds": 241.99,
      "end_seconds": 242.75,
      "duration_seconds": 0.76,
      "text": "Okay, noted."
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0038",
      "speaker_id": "person_2",
      "role": "DOCTOR",
      "start_seconds": 243.81,
      "end_seconds": 245.53,
      "duration_seconds": 1.72,
      "text": "Can I examine you now?"
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0039",
      "speaker_id": "person_3",
      "role": "PATIENT",
      "start_seconds": 246.96,
      "end_seconds": 247.66,
      "duration_seconds": 0.7,
      "text": "Alright."
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0040",
      "speaker_id": "person_2",
      "role": "DOCTOR",
      "start_seconds": 249.46,
      "end_seconds": 251.97,
      "duration_seconds": 2.51,
      "text": "Tell me if anything hurts as I press."
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0041",
      "speaker_id": "person_2",
      "role": "DOCTOR",
      "start_seconds": 270.46,
      "end_seconds": 275.41,
      "duration_seconds": 4.95,
      "text": "The tummy is soft, a little tender in the lower part, and there's no mass."
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0042",
      "speaker_id": "person_2",
      "role": "DOCTOR",
      "start_seconds": 276.77,
      "end_seconds": 278.12,
      "duration_seconds": 1.35,
      "text": "Let me press here."
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0043",
      "speaker_id": "person_2",
      "role": "DOCTOR",
      "start_seconds": 293.51,
      "end_seconds": 295.05,
      "duration_seconds": 1.54,
      "text": "You look a little pale."
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0044",
      "speaker_id": "person_2",
      "role": "DOCTOR",
      "start_seconds": 298.05,
      "end_seconds": 307.95,
      "duration_seconds": 9.9,
      "text": "All done, thank you, please sit down. Good, that's all I need to examine. Let me gather my thoughts and then we'll talk it through together."
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0045",
      "speaker_id": "person_2",
      "role": "DOCTOR",
      "start_seconds": 308.64,
      "end_seconds": 311.46,
      "duration_seconds": 2.82,
      "text": "One moment, the system's being slow today."
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0046",
      "speaker_id": "person_3",
      "role": "PATIENT",
      "start_seconds": 311.79,
      "end_seconds": 312.68,
      "duration_seconds": 0.89,
      "text": "That's alright."
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0047",
      "speaker_id": "person_2",
      "role": "DOCTOR",
      "start_seconds": 328.15,
      "end_seconds": 349.61,
      "duration_seconds": 21.46,
      "text": "Okay, here we go. Putting it all together, it fits best with heavy periods with a cause still to find. The reason I say that is that your story and my examination fit together. I'd also keep fibroids in mind. Let me just recap so I've got it right. You've had very heavy periods for about four days, and no fever or pain during sex."
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0048",
      "speaker_id": "person_3",
      "role": "PATIENT",
      "start_seconds": 350.21,
      "end_seconds": 351.44,
      "duration_seconds": 1.23,
      "text": "Yes, that's right."
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0049",
      "speaker_id": "person_2",
      "role": "DOCTOR",
      "start_seconds": 352.48,
      "end_seconds": 364.83,
      "duration_seconds": 12.35,
      "text": "Just so you know how the rest of the visit will go: I'll finish my notes, we'll agree on the plan, and the front desk will help with anything that needs booking. You shouldn't need to chase anything yourself."
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0050",
      "speaker_id": "person_3",
      "role": "PATIENT",
      "start_seconds": 365.9,
      "end_seconds": 369.17,
      "duration_seconds": 3.27,
      "text": "Good, I was wondering how this would go."
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0051",
      "speaker_id": "person_2",
      "role": "DOCTOR",
      "start_seconds": 369.92,
      "end_seconds": 372.36,
      "duration_seconds": 2.44,
      "text": "Let's get blood tests, for heavy periods."
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0052",
      "speaker_id": "person_3",
      "role": "PATIENT",
      "start_seconds": 373.24,
      "end_seconds": 375.67,
      "duration_seconds": 2.43,
      "text": "Alright. When can I do that?"
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0053",
      "speaker_id": "person_2",
      "role": "DOCTOR",
      "start_seconds": 376.36,
      "end_seconds": 381.63,
      "duration_seconds": 5.27,
      "text": "We should do a pregnancy test for abnormal bleeding. Any scans or blood work done already?"
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0054",
      "speaker_id": "person_3",
      "role": "PATIENT",
      "start_seconds": 382.52,
      "end_seconds": 389.07,
      "duration_seconds": 6.55,
      "text": "I did have a pelvic ultrasound done a few months ago, but the paper's at home."
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0055",
      "speaker_id": "person_2",
      "role": "DOCTOR",
      "start_seconds": 390.67,
      "end_seconds": 403.14,
      "duration_seconds": 12.47,
      "text": "I'm prescribing tranexamic acid, 500 milligrams, three times a day during periods, for three cycles. You take it by mouth. That should help with heavy bleeding. The pharmacy will go through the details again when you pick it up."
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0056",
      "speaker_id": "person_3",
      "role": "PATIENT",
      "start_seconds": 403.87,
      "end_seconds": 407.24,
      "duration_seconds": 3.37,
      "text": "Right, alright, I'll pick it up today."
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0057",
      "speaker_id": "person_2",
      "role": "DOCTOR",
      "start_seconds": 411.46,
      "end_seconds": 431.74,
      "duration_seconds": 20.28,
      "text": "Keep a note of how many pads you use each day and the dates, it helps us a lot. Make sure you're drinking plenty of fluids, two to three litres a day if you can, and get proper rest. And please bring the latest prescription or the medicine boxes to the next visit, so we can settle the dose."
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0058",
      "speaker_id": "person_3",
      "role": "PATIENT",
      "start_seconds": 433.2,
      "end_seconds": 434.48,
      "duration_seconds": 1.28,
      "text": "Okay, I will."
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0059",
      "speaker_id": "person_2",
      "role": "DOCTOR",
      "start_seconds": 435.74,
      "end_seconds": 444.98,
      "duration_seconds": 9.24,
      "text": "Keep an eye out, and if you soak through a pad every hour or feel faint, call us the same day or go to emergency."
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0060",
      "speaker_id": "person_3",
      "role": "PATIENT",
      "start_seconds": 445.97,
      "end_seconds": 447.86,
      "duration_seconds": 1.89,
      "text": "Got it, thank you."
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0061",
      "speaker_id": "person_2",
      "role": "DOCTOR",
      "start_seconds": 448.48,
      "end_seconds": 457.47,
      "duration_seconds": 8.99,
      "text": "Please come and see me in four weeks. Tell me what you've taken from all that, so I can fill in any gaps."
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0062",
      "speaker_id": "person_3",
      "role": "PATIENT",
      "start_seconds": 458.47,
      "end_seconds": 468.38,
      "duration_seconds": 9.91,
      "text": "So, I take the tranexamic acid, 500 milligrams, three times a day during periods and come back in four weeks. Is that right?"
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0063",
      "speaker_id": "person_2",
      "role": "DOCTOR",
      "start_seconds": 469.34,
      "end_seconds": 474.06,
      "duration_seconds": 4.72,
      "text": "Okay, yes, exactly right. Alright, that's everything from me. Any other questions?"
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0064",
      "speaker_id": "person_3",
      "role": "PATIENT",
      "start_seconds": 475.58,
      "end_seconds": 478.12,
      "duration_seconds": 2.54,
      "text": "No, you've explained it well. Thanks."
    }
  ]
}